    "method": "Each factor is the OWID-published per-product total from the ghg-per-kg-poore grapher CSV (Poore & Nemecek 2018 as republished by Our World in Data). For the five cooking oils, which the totals chart omits, the central value is the sum of that product's stage columns in the food-emissions-supply-chain grapher CSV; all other stage sums were verified this session to reproduce the totals chart, and the Shrimps (farmed) stage sum (26.8659) reproduces the Prawns (farmed) total (26.87). OWID publishes a single central value per product (verified: the ghg-per-kg-poore CSV has one value column and the food-footprints explorer serves the same columns; no per-product min/max is republished), and the per-product study ranges exist only inside the Poore & Nemecek (2018) supplementary materials, which are not published as an open per-product table. Therefore low = high = central for every factor and every factor carries rangeBasis 'point'. Ingredient-key mappings are listed one line each where the mapping is not 1:1.",
